{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"A serious regression — segfaults everywhere (stack overflow from infinite recursion). My `resolve_expr_path` change evaluates `:@=` tree args, and the std root `.caos-expr` (a deep-deps transform) uses `--in:@=.` — evaluating `.` re-runs the same expression forever. This is exactly the worker-vs-data ambiguity I worried about: `--in:@=.` is *data*, not a worker to evaluate.\n\nLet me revert the tree-eval (keep the safe `/std/` marking and the curry-result marking, which don't recurse):","type":"text"},{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01VSDj57Uj64MVzanMqSN21E","input":{"file_path":"crates/caos/src/eval.rs","new_string":"/// Resolve a `:@=` path value to a tree entry. A `/std/<name>` builtin is a\n/// worker reference — evaluated and marked (so an embedder becomes per-user).\n/// A path within `input_tree` is taken as-is (a raw reference): we can't tell a\n/// worker dir from a data dir by type, and blindly evaluating would re-run the\n/// container's own `.caos-expr` on a self/ancestor reference like `--in:@=.`\n/// (infinite recursion). Marking embedded *tree-path* workers awaits a\n/// worker-vs-data distinction (design/secrets.md, caller-propagation).\nfn resolve_expr_path(\n    t: &dyn Transport,\n    input_tree: &str,\n    value: &str,\n    store: &[ClientSecret],\n) -> Result<(EntryMode, gix::ObjectId), String> {\n    if let Some(name) = value.strip_prefix(\"/std/\") {\n        let hash = resolve_std_image(t, name)?;\n        let marked = mark_arg_tree(t, store, &hash)?;\n        return Ok((EntryKind::Tree.into(), parse_oid(&marked)?));\n    }\n    lookup_in_tree(t, input_tree, value)?\n        .ok_or_else(|| format!(\"eval-path: path {value:?} not found in tree\"))\n}","old_string":"/// Resolve a `:@=` path value to a tree entry. A worker reference is evaluated\n/// (so it carries its `secret-hash` mark and the embedder becomes per-user); a\n/// data reference is taken as-is. Cases: a `/std/<name>` builtin (evaluated and\n/// marked); a path within `input_tree` that is a directory (evaluated as an\n/// arg tree — its *own* `.caos-expr`, not the container's — and marked); a data\n/// blob/tree (referenced unchanged).\nfn resolve_expr_path(\n    t: &dyn Transport,\n    input_tree: &str,\n    value: &str,\n    store: &[ClientSecret],\n) -> Result<(EntryMode, gix::ObjectId), String> {\n    if let Some(name) = value.strip_prefix(\"/std/\") {\n        let hash = resolve_std_image(t, name)?;\n        let marked = mark_arg_tree(t, store, &hash)?;\n        return Ok((EntryKind::Tree.into(), parse_oid(&marked)?));\n    }\n    let (mode, oid) = lookup_in_tree(t, input_tree, value)?\n        .ok_or_else(|| format!(\"eval-path: path {value:?} not found in tree\"))?;\n    // A directory may be a worker: evaluate it starting AT its own subtree (so\n    // its `.caos-expr`, if any, runs — never the container's), which marks a\n    // curry/run result. A plain data dir with no `.caos-expr` comes back\n    // unchanged; a blob is data, referenced as-is.\n    if mode.is_tree() {\n        let (kind, evaluated) = eval_path(t, &oid.to_string(), \".\", store)?;\n        return Ok((mode_of_kind(&kind), parse_oid(&evaluated)?));\n    }\n    Ok((mode, oid))\n}"},"name":"edit","type":"tool_use"}],"results":[{"content":[{"text":"build (13s)\ntests (101s)\n  ✓ bash-tool       3s  2e7692561a3eeb429e7cb3686922deeb31e65e07\n  ! caos-tools     15s  b45c5aefd650b7aa5efb6c8182d0f0a2a5b5efab\n  ✓ cargo-check     2s  a00a45474b4e221111ea40a40341d241d5e3f141\n  ✓ cargo-crates   18s  1d505a5f216acb5ec027b9eff2c50c234f89bffa\n  ✓ cargo-self     17s  60ffc55a62aa4898f5dd314298b80ef95c6e58d5\n  ! chat-offline   16s  635c028e8c0d5be9e193adc95f15be3c64342a55\n  ✓ chat-online     0s  a68f3a8afd6c8f4722ddc95b4158c9ce560469cf\n  ✓ commit         13s  d946b1a15db4c47cfc173c505f7fc88760a13c4b\n  ✗ deep-deps      20s  fc79e5e2e78429b4af0bfd46b12d3f2ceafd6a20\n  ✓ dirs-only      13s  de032036096